notes=[
 '147-062-N1. The manuscript continues a discussion of the modular curve over the marked moduli space, with four named sections and an S4 action exchanging them. It says the construction will not be carried out here and would produce the unmarked modular multiplicities. These are manuscript claims; this page reading does not establish them mathematically.',
 '147-062-N2. The manuscript replaces diagram (76) by numerical diagram (78), with a codimension-zero vertex labeled 4 and a codimension-one two-vertex graph labeled 2,2, linked by an arrow labeled 1. It states that the unmarked space has a single point at infinity corresponding to the three points at infinity of the marked space, permuted transitively by S4. No independent proof of the quotient or its cusp count was performed.',
 '147-062-N3. Under the heading on fractional Euler–Poincaré characteristics, the manuscript writes the first two characteristic values −1 and 2, then a quotient-style characteristic and a decomposition using the exceptional sets {−bar j,−j} and {1/2,2,−1}. It ends with −1+1/3+1/2=−1/(24|6), with the denominator overwritten and unresolved. The separate NB writes division of chi_!(U an) by [S4], with result −1/24. The geometric equalities and any weighting convention were not independently proved.',
 '147-062-N4. A targeted exact-rational calculation in Python fractions.Fraction gives −1+1/3+1/2=−1/6, which differs from −1/24 by −1/8. Thus a final denominator 24 would make the displayed numerical equality false as written. The transcription preserves the written terms and the denominator doubt. This calculation neither supplies an omitted factor nor settles the overworked digits; no claim is made that all summands should be divided by 24.',
 'Source forms retained include Je vais pas without ne, the future form donnera, literal du = coup, the abbreviations pt/pts and EP, and the final point-set contribution’s curved ) with no comma before S4. The malformed delimiter is not silently balanced.',
 'Physical-lines count: 28. This comprises 19 main prose/formula baselines (the first characteristic formula shares the trouve baseline), two rows of diagram (78), one interlinear multiplicités insertion, four NB-margin baselines including its heading and formula, and the two isolated page/foliation numerals. Canceled words share their host baselines. Superscripts, subscripts, and the values/equality marks below g and nu are counted with their formulas.',
 'The full scan and both native halves were read against C and H, including every deletion, insertion, index, formula and margin. Nineteen actual reading places were cropped and viewed. One additional failed upper-right header search was saved and viewed, then renamed 147_scan062_search15.png; the number was found in the disjoint crop16 at x810–880, y25–70. The failed search is preserved but is not counted as a reading place. No OCR, web research, or TeX compilation was used.',
 'The ornate X alphabet remains unresolved. C’s calligraphic representation is preferred in each in-text doubt, with H’s fraktur representation retained as the alternative; three comparison rows record the preferred calligraphic representation against H, while no clear alphabet resolution or settled witness error is asserted. The U/P doubt likewise remains open. Only the visible paired stems change the font of its P alternative from bold to double-stroked; this alone is not counted as a substantive C change.',
 'H’s editorial introductory page label and its explanatory final note are not source ink. The author’s 30 and the separate pale 61 are transcribed by their appropriate distinct macros. The uncertain canceled decorations over M, absent from MARKS, are in doubts; decisions contains exactly M1035–M1038.',
 f'Coverage totals: {len(changes)} substantive comparison rows, {sum(x["against_C"] for x in changes)} against C and {sum(x["against_H"] for x in changes)} against H (a row can concern both); four indexed decisions, of which two first readings resolve and two remain undecided. Added certainty-only doubts are excluded from the change count.'
]

